    "description": "Notion | Retrieve a page's content as Markdown. Accepts a block ID as well as a page ID, so a single section can be read on its own instead of fetching a whole large page. On a page you have not read before, start with \`format: outline\` to get the headings and their block IDs cheaply, then read only the section you need. The Markdown returned is display-oriented: escaping of characters such as \`*\`, \`~\` and \`#\` may differ from what is stored, so it is not guaranteed to round-trip when fed back as \`old_str\`. For edits that must be precise, address blocks by ID via Retrieve block children instead.
Error Responses:
400: Bad request
